section class='flex-1 flex flex-col' aria-label=label
  / A list without a switch, a filter, sums or a map has no head
  - if head?
    / The head keeps the height of the button of the map, also without it, so
      the list does not move with a switch to a list without a map. On the
      desktop it is a tinted band over the full width of the white page, and
      its content stays in line with the rows below. On a phone it stays while
      the next list loads, so only the list changes.
    div class='ui-keep-lit flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-3 gap-y-2 max-lg:mb-5 lg:flex-nowrap lg:gap-5 lg:min-h-18.5 lg:-mx-6 lg:-mt-5 lg:mb-2 lg:pl-9 lg:pr-11 lg:py-4 lg:rounded-t-lg lg:bg-indigo-50 dark:lg:bg-slate-800/70'
      - if segments.any?
        .max-lg:w-full.max-lg:min-h-10.max-lg:flex.max-lg:items-center
          = render Ui::SegmentedControl::Component.new(items: segments, label:, stretch: true)
      / The filter of the list, like a place, follows the switch
      - if filter?
        = filter
      / A switch like the one of the sessions to review, the sums, and on a
        phone the icon of the map at their end. The icon has the size of the
        text, so the line keeps its height with or without the map, and the
        switch of the lists above keeps its width.
      - if totals.present? || map_button? || switch?
        div class=['flex flex-wrap items-center justify-center lg:justify-end gap-x-2.5 gap-y-2 max-lg:w-full lg:ml-auto', (stats.any? ? 'max-lg:mt-2' : 'max-lg:px-1')]
          - if switch?
            / A phone has the switch in a line of its own below the sums
            div class='lg:mr-3 max-lg:order-last max-lg:w-full max-lg:flex max-lg:justify-center' = switch
          - if totals.present?
            span.text-sm.lg:text-base.text-fg-secondary.tabular-nums class=('max-lg:hidden' if stats.any?) title=totals_note data-controller=('tooltip' if totals_note) data-tooltip-touch-value=('true' if totals_note) = totals_html
          / The sums of a phone as columns in a card, each value above its caption
          - if stats.any?
            div class='lg:hidden w-full grid rounded-xl bg-surface py-3 divide-x divide-line text-center' style="grid-template-columns: repeat(#{stat_columns}, minmax(0, 1fr))"
              - stats.each do |stat|
                div class='flex min-w-0 flex-col' title=stat.note data-controller=('tooltip' if stat.note) data-tooltip-touch-value=('true' if stat.note)
                  span.text-lg.font-semibold.leading-tight.tabular-nums.whitespace-nowrap.text-fg = stat.value
                  span.truncate.text-sm.text-muted = stat.caption
              - if map_button?
                = link_to map_path, class: 'flex min-w-0 flex-col items-center rounded text-indigo-600 dark:text-indigo-400 focus-ring click-animation', title: map_label, aria: { label: map_label }, data: { turbo_frame: map_frame } do
                  span.text-lg.leading-tight = icon 'map'
                  span.truncate.text-sm = t('.map')
          - elsif map_button?
            = link_to map_path, class: 'lg:hidden relative inline-flex items-center text-indigo-600 dark:text-indigo-400 touch-target focus-ring rounded', title: map_label, aria: { label: map_label }, data: { controller: 'tooltip', turbo_frame: map_frame } do
              = icon 'map'
      - if map_button?
        div class=['max-lg:hidden', ('ml-auto' if totals.blank?)]
          = render Ui::Button::Component.new(href: map_path, style: :secondary, icon: 'map', label: t('.map'), data: { turbo_frame: map_frame })

    / The map fills the window over the list (see Car::MapOverlay::Component).
      A link in its tooltip leaves the list.
    - if map_path
      = helpers.turbo_frame_tag map_frame, target: '_top'

  - notes.each do |note|
    div class='max-lg:mb-4 max-lg:px-1 lg:px-5 lg:py-3 lg:border-b lg:border-line'
      = note

  = content
